<Base title="Privacy Policy — Pegboard Seven"
      description="What Pegboard Seven stores and what it sends. In this version, nothing leaves your phone."
      current="legal">

  <section>
    <p class="kicker">Pegboard Seven · Privacy Policy</p>
    <h1 style="max-width:22ch">Nothing leaves your phone.</h1>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="prose">
<p>
  Pegboard Seven is a game. It has no accounts, no sign-in, no messaging and no
  profile. We never ask for your name, your email address or your location, and
  there is nowhere in the app to type any of them.
</p>
<p>
  This page describes <strong>version 1.0</strong>, the version on the App Store
  today. It is short because the app is short: it does not send anything
  anywhere.
</p>

<h2>Who is responsible</h2>
<p>
  The data controller is <strong>Nurçin Ehlimanoğlu</strong>, a sole
  proprietorship registered in Türkiye, reachable at
  <a href="mailto:nehlimanoglu@gmail.com">nehlimanoglu@gmail.com</a>. There is
  no data protection officer: the business is one person, and that person reads
  the address above.
</p>

<h2>What stays on your device</h2>
<p>
  Your progress is saved on the phone itself, using Apple's standard storage
  (<code>UserDefaults</code>). It never leaves the device and we cannot read it.
  It holds exactly this:
</p>
<ul>
  <li>which levels you have unlocked, and the stars on each one</li>
  <li>your coin balance, and whether you own the ad-free upgrade</li>
  <li>daily-reward streak and the date it was last claimed</li>
  <li>weekly event progress and which rewards you have taken</li>
  <li>which chapter briefings you have already been shown</li>
  <li>your sound and haptics settings</li>
</ul>
<p>
  Deleting the app deletes all of it. Purchases are the exception — they live
  with your Apple ID rather than with us, so they survive a reinstall and can be
  restored from the shop.
</p>

<h2>What the app sends</h2>
<p>
  <strong>Nothing.</strong> This version contains no analytics, no crash
  reporting, no advertising and no tracking. The game code makes no network
  requests of its own; there is no server behind it and no account to sync to.
</p>
<p>
  Because there is no advertising, the app does not use the Advertising
  Identifier (IDFA) and <strong>never shows the App Tracking Transparency
  prompt</strong>. If you have seen that prompt, it did not come from this app.
</p>

<h2>Purchases</h2>
<p>
  The shop sells two coin packs. The purchase itself is carried out entirely by
  <strong>Apple</strong>: you pay Apple, Apple verifies the receipt, and Apple
  tells the app whether it succeeded. We never see your card details, your Apple
  ID or your billing address — none of that reaches us, and there is no place in
  the app where it could.
</p>
<p>
  What Apple does with that transaction is covered by Apple's own privacy
  policy, where Apple is the controller and we are not.
</p>

<h2>Why we are allowed to do this</h2>
<p>
  We do not process personal data, so the usual machinery — legal bases,
  profiling, data sharing — has nothing to attach to. Saving your progress on
  your own device is not processing by us; we cannot see it and it is not sent
  anywhere. The only processing connected to the app is Apple's handling of a
  purchase, which Apple performs to fulfil the contract you make with Apple.
</p>

<h2>Children</h2>
<p>
  The game collects nothing from anyone, so there is no children's data to
  handle differently. There is no chat, no user-generated content, no external
  links inside gameplay, and no advertising.
</p>

<h2>Your rights</h2>
<p>
  Rights of access, correction, deletion, objection and portability exist under
  the GDPR, the UK GDPR and Türkiye's KVKK (Law 6698). They apply to data we
  hold about you — and we hold none, which means there is nothing to hand over
  and nothing to erase. Deleting the app removes the on-device save.
</p>
<p>
  If you believe that is wrong, write to
  <a href="mailto:nehlimanoglu@gmail.com">nehlimanoglu@gmail.com</a>. You may
  also complain directly to a supervisory authority — your national authority in
  the EEA, the ICO in the UK, or the Personal Data Protection Authority (KVKK)
  in Türkiye — without contacting us first.
</p>

<h2>If this changes</h2>
<p>
  Analytics, crash reporting and advertising are all things this game may gain
  in a later version. None of them can be switched on quietly: each one changes
  what the app sends, and <strong>this page is updated before that version
  ships</strong>, together with the App Store privacy label. The date below tells
  you which version you are reading about.
</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>
  <a href="mailto:nehlimanoglu@gmail.com">nehlimanoglu@gmail.com</a> — replies
  within three working days.
</p>

<p class="fine">
  Applies to Pegboard Seven version 1.0. Last updated 10 September 2026.
</p>
    </div>
  </section>

